SUMMARY:Pluralities Project: “The Negro Artist” Screening & Live Award
 s
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T203000
DTSTAMP:20261103T193658Z
UID:funcheap-1643697@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Movies
DESCRIPTION:Nik HeftmanPluralities Project: “The Negro Artist” Screeni
 ng & Live Awards\nJoin the Documentary Film Institute at San Francisco Sta
 te University on Thursday\, November 5\, 2026\, at 5:30 PM at McKenna Thea
 tre for the closing-night event of the sixth Pluralities Project. The even
 ing features a screening of The Negro Artist\, presented by filmmaker Nik 
 Heftman and poet Caleb Rainey\, followed by the Accomplice Awards honoring
  artists\, activists\, and cultural figures who have brought important iss
 ues to light. This year’s posthumous honorees include pioneering Black j
 ournalist Belva Davis and her longtime producer George Osterkamp\, along w
 ith influential cultural critic\, musician\, and artist Greg Tate. Part of
  the sixth Pluralities Seminar\, this event brings together film\, poetry\
 , journalism\, and cultural history to celebrate the people who challenge 
 narratives and shape our understanding of the world.\nDate: Thursday\, Nov
 ember 5\, 2026\nTime: 5:30 PM\nLocation: McKenna Theatre\, San Francisco S
 tate University\, 1600 Holloway Avenue\, San Francisco\, CA 94132\n\nFree\
 n\nTickets: https://lcalive.org/public/events/3e2ea49a-f9f6-4664-bed4-a912
 ca158a58\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/pluralities-project-negro-artis
 t-screening-live-awards/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Screen
 shot-2026-10-21-at-10.33.26-AM.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261103T193658Z
LOCATION:McKenna Theatre\, San Francisco State University\, 1600 Holloway 
 Ave\, San Francisco\, CA 94132
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/pluralities-project-negro-artist-screening-liv
 e-awards/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:El Sett (Opening Night of the 30th Arab Film Festival)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T200000
DTSTAMP:20261106T110227Z
UID:dothebay-17998364@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:The 30th Arab Film Festival opens with Marwan Hamed’s sweepi
 ng portrait of Umm Kulthum\, the most iconic Arab singer of all time.\n\nB
 efore the film\, Guest of Honor Mohamed Hefzy receives the very first AFMI
  Luminary Award for Cultural Impact. After it\, Aswat Ensemble takes the s
 tage with a live tribute to her music.\n\nJoin us in your best evening att
 ire\, just as you would have dressed to see Umm Kulthum at her legendary 1
 967 concert at the Paris Olympia. There will be plenty of chances to have 
 your photo taken\, so let’s make the evening a tribute to the most iconi
 c Arab singer of all time.\n\nPlease note: Some scenes have a strobing eff
 ect that may affect photosensitive viewers.\n\nThe flagship event of the A
 rab Film and Media Institute (AFMI)\, the Arab Film Festival is the longes
 t running and largest independent festival of its kind in North America.\n
 \nThis year\, join us from Nov.5th to Nov 14th for a program that will spa
 n 10 days\, presenting over 40 films from 26 countries\, over 30 directed 
 by women. AFF30 will also include opportunities to get together\, a classi
 c film\, industry and community panels\, filmmaker Q&As and more. Select p
 rograms will also be simultaneously presented online.\n\nFor more details\
 , visit arabfilmfestival.org\n\nhttps://aff30.arabfilmfestival.org/events#
 opening-night\nThe 30th Arab Film Festival presents:\n\nDetails: https://d
 othebay.com/events/2026/11/5/el-sett-opening-night-of-the-30th-arab-film-f
 estival-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funchea
 p.com/30th-arab-film-festival-sfs-amc-kabuki-nov-514/
GEO:37.7849834;-122.4326374
