 et/34611227/dbcb1877-9a98-4fac-9345-63e6a7eeccf7.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261107T102259Z
LOCATION:Brava Theater\, 2781 24th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94110
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/6/robert-shields-my-life-as-a-robo
 t-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Littermates
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T214500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T234500
DTSTAMP:20261107T102259Z
UID:dothebay-18008033@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:At Chester’s cottage\, good behavior earns karaoke. Getting 
 answers is a little more complicated.\n\nAfter a mysterious apocalyptic(is
 h) attack leaves them bloodied\, disoriented\, and unable to speak\, Liam 
 (Joey Bader) and Mel (Kaylee McGregor) take refuge in the English countrys
 ide. Their oddball host\, Chester (Oliver Woolf)\, feeds them\, helps them
  recover\, and introduces a system of rewards: behave yourself\, earn “n
 ifties\,” cash them in for hot-tub time and dance parties.\n\nBeyond the
  cottage\, things are less nifty. But within it\, a makeshift family is ta
 king shape. While Liam embraces their new life\, Mel grows increasingly cu
 rious about the world Chester insists is too dangerous to enter…\n\nIn t
 heir feature debut\, directors Scott Tinkham and Michael Woloson mix deadp
 an comedy\, sibling rivalry\, and creeping unease in a coming-of-age story
  about people who have to grow up all over again. Winner of the Special Ju
 ry Prize at the 2026 Manchester Film Festival and the Narrative Feature Au
 dience Award at Dances With Films LA 2026\, this has the sort of sensibili
 ties that fans of Yorgos Lanthimos and Ben Wheatley will adore… and it
 ’s a natural fit as an Alamo Exclusive.\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com
 /events/2026/11/6/littermates-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
