DESCRIPTION:The finale of the Studio 8 Film Festival. The 2026 Legacy Awar
 d honors Dutch filmmaker Babeth Mondini VanLoo (SFAI\, 1977)\, a student o
 f Joseph Beuys whose documentaries span five decades\, from punk to Buddhi
 sm.\nProgram: Berlin Wall and the Sex Pistols (1978)\, Arnold Schwarzenegg
 er: The Art of Bodybuilding (1975–2019)\, Not Guilty: For Keith Richards
  (1977\, with Abel Ferrara)\, and Chance Versus Causality (1976–79). Fol
 lowed by the Legacy Award presentation and a conversation with San Francis
 co-based curator Tanya Zimbardo.\nCurated by Marian Wallace with the filmm
 aker. Part of Studio 8 Film Festival\, Nov 6 to 8: Juror Night (Fri\, 7:30
  PM) and Juried Show: Personal Visions (Sat\, 2 PM) at the 4-Star Theater.
  Weekend Pass $30.\n\n$15 ($30 supporter ticket)\, all ages\nSF Artists Al
 umni presents:\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/8/studio-8-
 film-festival-2026-legacy-award-for-babeth-mondini-vanloo-tickets\nSource:
