BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hold on to Your Music: A Mother's Legacy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T190000
DTSTAMP:20261109T114430Z
UID:dothebay-17956737@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the San Francisco premiere of Hold On To Your Musi
 c: A Mother's Legacy\, including a live performance by internationally acc
 laimed concert pianist Mona Golabek.\n\nVienna\, 1938. The parents of 14-y
 ear-old piano prodigy Lisa Jura faced an unimaginable choice: which of the
 ir three daughters to send to safety on the Kindertransport. They chose Li
 sa. She arrived alone in London\, carrying her dreams\, memories of her fa
 mily\, and her mother's parting words: "Hold on to your music."\n\nDirecte
 d by Academy Award nominated Josh Aronson and Emmy Award winner Adam Wood\
 , the film tells Lisa's remarkable story through rare archival footage\, n
 ewly restored recordings\, and performances by her daughter\, Mona Golabek
 . Drawing on Golabek's best-selling book and acclaimed stage production\, 
 The Pianist of Willesden Lane\, it celebrates the enduring power of music 
 and a mother's love - a story that has reached more than 20 million people
  worldwide.\n\nFollowing the screening and live performance\, Golabek join
 s director Josh Aronson and producer Susan Solomon Libitzky in conversatio
 n with executive producer\, Dr. Anita Friedman.\n\n$30.\n\nPresented by JC
 C SF\n\n$30.\nJCC SF\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/8/hol
 d-on-to-your-music-a-mother-s-legacy-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.787374;-122.4473551
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34962749/d3229d73-be80-448c-ae4d-f9ed0e5d0864.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261109T114430Z
LOCATION:Jewish Community Center of San Francisco\, 3200 California Street
 \, San Francisco\, CA\, 94118
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/8/hold-on-to-your-music-a-mother-s
 -legacy-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Edward Said: Between Worlds (Bay Area Premiere)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T174500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T194500
DTSTAMP:20261109T114430Z
UID:dothebay-17998256@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:As part of the 30th Arab Film Festival\, join us for the Bay A
 rea Premiere of Edward Said: Between Worlds\, an archival documentary exam
 ining the life\, ideas\, and enduring legacy of Palestinian-American schol
 ar\, author\, and public intellectual Edward Said.\n\nTold through archiva
 l material and Said’s own words\, the film follows his journey from his 
 childhood in Jerusalem and displacement in 1948 through his academic caree
 r at Columbia University and his emergence as one of the twentieth century
 ’s most influential cultural critics and advocates for the Palestinian p
 eople.\n\nStay after the film for a panel discussion with director Maiken 
 Baird\, producer Sarah Mowaswes\, and Edward Said’s family\, moderated b
 y Dr. Ussama Makdisi.\n\nThis screening is co-sponsored by the Palestinian
  & Arab Studies Program at UC Berkeley.\n\nThe flagship event of the Arab 
 Film and Media Institute (AFMI)\, the Arab Film Festival is the longest ru
 nning and largest independent festival of its kind in North America.\n\nTh
 is year\, join us from Nov.5th to Nov 14th for a program that will span 10
  days\, presenting over 40 films from 26 countries\, over 30 directed by w
 omen.\n\nAFF30 will also include opportunities to get together\, a classic
  film\, industry and community panels\, filmmaker Q&As and more. Select pr
 ograms will also be simultaneously presented online.\n\nFor more details\,
  visit arabfilmfestival.org\n\nhttps://aff30.arabfilmfestival.org/events#c
 enterpiece\nThe Arab Film Festival presents:\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.
 com/events/2026/11/8/edward-said-between-worlds-bay-area-premiere-tickets\
 nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.761992;-122.434743
