UID:dothebay-18016726@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:FATHERLAND centres on the relationship between the Nobel Prize
 -winning writer Thomas Mann (Hanns Zischler) and his daughter Erika (Sandr
 a Hüller) – actress\, writer and rally driver. In the summer of 1949\, 
 at the height of the Cold War\, father and daughter embark on a challengin
 g and emotional road trip in a black Buick taking them across a Germany in
  ruins – from US dominated Frankfurt to Soviet controlled Weimar. Return
 ing home after sixteen years of exile in the US\, Thomas Mann has to face 
 not only a divided fatherland\, but also a deep fracture within his own fa
 mily.\n\nWith FATHERLAND\, director Paweł Pawlikowski picks up where he l
 eft off with his award-winning IDA and COLD WAR\, exploring – in his ell
 iptic\, distilled style – the themes of identity\, family\, love and gui
 lt amid the turmoil and confusion of post-war Europe.\n\n“Another expans
 ive\, enriching work from a modern master” – Time Out\n\n“A rich and
  moving journey through post-World War II Germany” – TheWrap\n\nMore s
 howtimes will be added soon.\n\nRuntime\n\n1h 22m\n\nYear\n\n2026\n\nDirec
 tor\n\nPaweł Pawlikowski\n\nFormat\n\nDCP\n\nCountry\n\nPoland\, Germany\
 , Italy & France\n\nLanguage\n\nGerman\, French\, Russian & English\n\nFir
 st Showing\n\nNovember 6\, 2026\n\nCategories\n\nOpen Caption Screenings\n
 \n\,\n\nFeatured\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/2
 2479?siteToken=4m48btf3yavn7xjk5yxk6nc40c\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/e
 vents/2026/11/9/fatherland-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
