DESCRIPTION:From two-time Palme d’Or winner Cristian Mungiu\, a Norwegia
 n woman and her devout\n\nRomanian husband relocate with their five childr
 en to a remote\, close-knit\, coastal town. Their\n\nteenage children form
  a fast bond with a neighboring family as unease begins to simmer around\n
 \ntheir rigid beliefs. When allegations of abuse emerge\, they are forced 
 to confront a system of\n\njudgment that blurs the line between concern an
 d prejudice.\n\n“It is a treat to be in the hands of a director with suc
 h skill for image-making.” – Sophie Kaufman\, BFI\n\n“Fjord explores
  clashing worldviews\, conformity\, tolerance and the boundaries of freedo
 m and intimacy.” – Eye Eye Pictures\n\nRuntime\n\n2h 26m\n\nYear\n\n20
 26\n\nDirector\n\nCristian Mungiu\n\nFormat\n\nDCP\n\nCountry\n\nRomania\n
