BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sftff 2026 – Speculative Fiction
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T210000
DTSTAMP:20261109T114430Z
UID:dothebay-17988725@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:The 2026 San Francisco Transgender Film Festival continues wit
 h SPECULATIVE FICTION\, a shorts block featuring six out of this world fil
 ms.\n\nLas Cosas Que Brillan (11:09min)\n\nKristal Sotomayor\, United Stat
 es\, 2025\n\nA curious trans mermaid defies her mother’s warnings to ven
 ture up to the surface\, only to discover the world above is not what she 
 dreamt. Las Cosas Que Brillan explores the impacts of environmental destru
 ction\, and the danger of being desired in a postcolonial world.\n\nMother
 hood (12:22min)\n\nAva Corder\, United States\, 2025\n\nNicki is one of th
 e first trans women to carry a baby to term as part of a groundbreaking ut
 erine transplant trial. Just hours before her scheduled C-section\, her wa
 ter breaks—something the doctors said couldn’t happen. Her physician u
 rges her to stick to protocol\, warning that the outcome of her birth coul
 d impact access for future trans patients. Her husband\, Benny\, and her f
 ather\, Al\, beg her to comply. But Nicki chooses to follow her instinct a
 nd pursue a natural birth at home. She’ll give birth on her terms.\n\nLo
 ng Away (16:32min)\n\nTilly Bridges & Susan Bridges\, United States\, 2025
 \n\nSet twenty-five years into the future\, Long Away is a sci-fi story ab
 out Victoria and the father who died when she was very young. As a trans w
 oman who transitioned as an adult\, Victoria’s father never got to know 
 her truth. She uses a one-round-trip-only time travel device to jump back 
 to our present and meet the man she can barely remember… and try to find
  out...\n\nTickets: https://sftff2026.eventive.org/schedule/tickets/6a760f
 b1dc6a19eb0d654d7b\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/14/sftff-
 2026-speculative-fiction-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- h
 ttps://dancersgroup.org/calendar/29th-anniversary-san-francisco-transgende
 r-film-festival/2026-11-14/1/?utm_source=caldiscovery&utm_medium=ics&utm_c
 ampaign=san-francisco-ca
GEO:37.7647103;-122.4224081
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35107385/fbf84e23-8298-430a-ae9a-62edb2e32aa1.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261109T114430Z
LOCATION:Roxie Theater\, 3117 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/14/sftff-2026-speculative-fiction-
 tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sftff 2026 – Adult (18+)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T210000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T230000
DTSTAMP:20261024T160225Z
UID:dothebay-17988726@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:The 2026 San Francisco Transgender Film Festival continues wit
 h ADULT(18+)\, a shorts block featuring five intimate and definitively adu
 lt films.\n\nMommy (8:40min)\n\nEvie Snax\, Manon Praline\, United States 
 & Germany\, 2024\n\nSix years after her bottom surgery\, Manon Praline sha
 res a moving testimony of the challenges and joys she encountered on that 
 journey. Her story is complemented with beautiful imagery shot by artist E
 va Wu in the dramatic landscape of the North American Southwest\, and scor
 ed by Pride Month Barbie’s musical sensation Josephine Shetty. This expe
 rimental documentary short is a sequel to the trio’s debut film Baby (20
 18) which has been shown at almost 40 film festivals throughout Europe and
  North America and received many praises.\n\nLike honey on the tongue of a
  sweet tooth\, Mommy pours pure honesty and vulnerability into the viewer
 ’s eyes\, ears\, and hearts.\n\nPossessions of the Spooky Kind (13:00min
 )\n\nIris Glitzer\, Officer Flower\, Germany\, 2025\n\nDuring a walk in th
 e woods\, two shy flatmates discover an abandoned clinic and get lost in i
 t. A ghost encounter makes their inhibitions disappear. Sometimes all it t
 akes is some paranormal activity to get closer to your crush.\n\nCrashPad 
 Series: J London and Johnny Castro (11:54min)\n\nAva LaPrima\, United Stat
 es\, 2025\n\n“Johnny Castro falls for London’s tower!“\n\nSlick stud
 s Johnny Castro and J London get kinky in the CrashPad. Blindfolded\, J ca
 n only focus on the pleasure of getting his ass eaten\, cock sucked\, and 
 holes fucke...\n\nTickets: https://sftff2026.eventive.org/schedule/tickets
 /6a760fbe8b0effeb415af206\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/14
 /sftff-2026-adult-18-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7647103;-122.4224081
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35107403/a9bba4a6-92b6-4d66-ab7d-e35d72a21af4.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261024T160225Z
LOCATION:Roxie Theater\, 3117 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/14/sftff-2026-adult-18-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hunting Flies + Roly Poly
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T170000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17923120@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Presented together\, Hunting Flies and Roly Poly are two disti
 nct satirical comedy films by celebrated Director Andrzej Wajda.\n\nHuntin
 g Flies will be preceded by the short film Roly Poly.\n\nRoly Poly – Run
 time: 35 minutes\n\nThe story of a racing car driver who undergoes so many
  transplants that it can no longer be determined which people have contrib
 uted to his make-up.\n\nRally driver Richard Fox keeps getting involved in
  terrible accidents but always manages to survive thanks to organs transpl
 anted from people who died in crashes he caused. The situation complicates
  when he starts acquiring his donors’ personality traits along with thei
 r organs.\n\nHunting Flies – Runtime: 104 minutes\n\nWlodek is a shy man
  who’s afraid of his mother as well as his wife. However\, upon meeting 
 Irena\, his life takes a new turn.\n\nOne of the key films of the Polish f
 ilm renaissance\, this satiric comedy explores the seeming world of emanci
 pated women and emasculated men in Communist Poland. A librarian shares hi
 s life and home with his domineering wife. He has an affair with a beautif
 ul intellectual\, who wears fly-shaped glasses. She tries to become the wo
 man behind the great artist. It’s a film dedicated to the women of Polan
 d\, even as it critiques the relations between the sexes.\n\nScreenings of
  Andrzej Wajda’s films in the USA in 2026 are part of the ‘Wajda 100 T
 our – North America’ project\, organized by DI Factory with the financ
 ial support of the Polish Film Institute.\n\nRuntime\n\n2h 19m\n\nYear\n\n
 1969\n\nD...\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/22250
 ?siteToken=4m48btf3yavn7xjk5yxk6nc40c\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/event
 s/2026/11/15/hunting-flies-roly-poly-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7647103;-122.4224081
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34800070/8d8cbcf1-5b12-4915-9325-385442cd112a.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:Roxie Theater\, 3117 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/15/hunting-flies-roly-poly-tickets
END:VEVENT
