DESCRIPTION:Advance screening followed by a Q&A with director Michał Marc
 zak on Thursday\, November 5\, at New People Cinema!\n\nAfter his teenage 
 son\, Chris\, is last seen by a surveillance camera on a bridge over Warsa
 w’s turbulent Vistula River\, Daniel embarks on an all-consuming search.
  Armed with self-built boats\, drones\, and underwater cameras\, he relent
 lessly scours the river’s depths. As months pass\, while his own family 
 struggles to live with the uncertainty of Chris’s disappearance\, Daniel
  begins helping other families with missing loved ones find answers — an
 d\, at times\, the closure that continues to elude him.\n\n“An ultra-imm
 ersive portrait of grief\, acceptance\, and the role that hope can play in
  delaying them.-IndieWire\n\n“One of the best documentaries of Sundance 
 2026.” – RogerEbert.com\n\nRuntime\n\n1h 48m\n\nYear\n\n2026\n\nDirect
 or\n\nMichał Marczak\n\nFormat\n\nDCP\n\nCountry\n\nPoland & France\n\nLa
 nguage\n\nPolish with English subtitles\n\nFirst Showing\n\nNovember 13\, 
 2026\n\nCategories\n\nFeatured\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.
 com/purchase/22450?siteToken=4m48btf3yavn7xjk5yxk6nc40c\nDetails: https://
 dothebay.com/events/2026/11/16/closure-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
