CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to Fear City: NYPD Surveillance Films from The Bureau 
 of Special Services\n\nThe NYPD Bureau of Special Services conducted cover
 t surveillance on political and social activists from 1960 to 1980\, captu
 ring on film activities of the Civil Rights Movement\, Vietnam War protest
 ors\, Cold War activists and many more developments of this politically tu
 multuous period. Now\, all 1\,450 films have been digitized and made publi
 cly available by the NYC Department of Records.\n\nThis special screening 
 features a small selection of these revealing films hosted by the former f
 ilm archivist from the NYC Department of Records who digitized and preserv
 ed these films. Join us for an open discussion and screening of the conten
 ts of these silent films where the audience is encouraged to pose their qu
 estions to the archivist who worked directly with these historic records.\
 n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/21/welcome-to-fear-city-ti
 ckets\nSource: DoTheBay
