DTSTAMP:20261023T171442Z
UID:dothebay-17979570@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Peter Greenaway's 1989 magnum opus THE COOK\, THE THIEF\, HIS 
 WIFE & HER LOVER is neo-noir for the hungry\, devious soul. Released at a 
 time when crime cinema was growing increasingly perverse with the likes of
  ANGEL HEART (1987)\, BLUE VELVET (1986)\, and BODY DOUBLE (1984)\, Greena
 way's film out-shocks the buch by intertwining two of human nature's favor
 ite pastimes: food and sex. Like Marco Ferreri's LA GRAND BOUFFE (1973) an
 d Paul Bartel's EATING RAOUL (1982) before it\, food and sex quickly turn 
 into a recipe for something decidedly more sinister and... cannibalistic. 
 Shocking audiences at the time of its release\, time has not tamed Greenaw
 ay's film at all\, and you'll never look at Helen Mirren or Michael Gambon
  the same way again. (Justin LaLiberty)\n\nDCP courtesy of Universal Pictu
 res\n\nTickets: https://drafthouse.com/sf/show/the-cook-the-thief-his-wife
 -her-lover?cinemaId=0802&sessionId=22958\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/ev
 ents/2026/11/24/the-cook-the-thief-his-wife-her-lover-tickets\nSource: DoT
 heBay
