DESCRIPTION:Steven Lisberger’s TRON plunges Jeff Bridges into a glowing 
 digital universe of programs\, gladiatorial games\, and machine logic\, cr
 eating one of the most distinctive visions of cyberspace ever put on scree
 n. Syd Mead’s concept work helped shape the film’s sleek vehicles and 
 futuristic environments\, bringing his precision and industrial imaginatio
 n to a world that felt radically new in 1982. Decades later\, TRON still l
 ooks like the future as dreamed by a graphic designer with the circuitry e
 xposed.\n\nPart of The Future According to Syd Mead\, presented in conjunc
 tion with Syd Mead: Future Pastime\, on view October 8 through December 17
 \, 2026 at San Francisco’s Transamerica Pyramid Annex Gallery.\n\nRuntim
 e\n\n1h 36m\n\nYear\n\n2025\n\nDirector\n\nSteven Lisberger\n\nFormat\n\nD
 CP\n\nFirst Showing\n\nDecember 11\, 2026\n\nCategories\n\nThe Future Acco
 rding to Syd Mead\n\n\,\n\nFeatured\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.v
 eezi.com/purchase/22255?siteToken=4m48btf3yavn7xjk5yxk6nc40c\nDetails: htt
 ps://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/11/tron-4k-restoration-tickets\nSource: D
 oTheBay
