SUMMARY:Carol
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261221T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261221T200000
DTSTAMP:20261102T193355Z
UID:dothebay-18016745@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Presented by OUTlook and Frameline\n\nDubbed “SF’s hottest
  new holiday tradition” by the San Francisco Chronicle\, Frameline’s f
 ourth annual Carol Day returns to its home at the Roxie Theater. Shake up 
 your martinis\, don your gloves (and gay apparel) for a costume contest\, 
 and get ready to be flung out of space — again.\n\nSet during Christmast
 ime in 1950s New York\, Todd Haynes’ adaptation of Patricia Highsmith’
 s The Price of Salt centers on shy\, aspiring photographer Therese Belivet
  (Rooney Mara)\, whose world changes when she meets the elegant Carol Aird
  (Cate Blanchett). As Carol struggles to maintain custody of her daughter 
 amid a heated divorce\, she and Therese develop a secret-yet-passionate ro
 mance that changes them both irrevocably.\n\nFeaturing a stunning screenpl
 ay from Phyllis Nagy\; memorable supporting turns from Sarah Paulson\, Kyl
 e Chandler\, and Jake Lacy\; and wholly transportive production design and
  costuming\, Carol remains one of queer cinema’s most exquisite films.\n
 \nRuntime\n\n1h 58m\n\nYear\n\n2015\n\nDirector\n\nTodd Haynes\n\nFormat\n
 \nDCP\n\nFirst Showing\n\nDecember 21\, 2026\n\nCategories\n\nOUTlook\n\n\
 ,\n\nFeatured\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/2245
 2?siteToken=4m48btf3yavn7xjk5yxk6nc40c\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/even
 ts/2026/12/21/carol-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7647103;-122.4224081
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35226407/bd640154-a746-457c-b427-3051960aaf3c.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261102T193355Z
LOCATION:Roxie Theater\, 3117 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/21/carol-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Apartment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261228T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261228T210000
DTSTAMP:20261029T100747Z
UID:dothebay-17979587@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:A young upstart\, C.C. Baxter (Jack Lemmon)\, will do anything
  to move up in the world...even loan out his apartment to the higher-ups f
 or their romantic flings and extramarital trysts. All seems relatively fin
 e and dandy until C.C. finds a romance of his own.\n\nBilly Wilder is a ge
 nius – there aren't enough words in the world to describe all the films 
 he's made and express how much he means to cinema – but in 1960\, Wilder
  wrote and directed a perfect movie. I'm not saying this to sell you on th
 e idea of seeing this film at the Alamo\; I'm stating it as a fact. There 
 are very few instances where you watch a movie and realize you are witness
 ing pure magnificence in that moment. Sometimes you think about a movie af
 ter the fact\, and it gets better and better until you begin to love a mov
 ie you previously only really liked. THE APARTMENT is NOT one of those mov
 ies. It is a movie where\, within 15 minutes of watching\, you realize it 
 is unlike anything you have ever seen before. Jack Lemmon is amazing\, Shi
 rley MacLaine is a full-on pixie dream girl\, and the chemistry and dialog
 ue snap and sparkle like you wouldn't believe.\n\nTickets: https://draftho
 use.com/sf/show/the-apartment?cinemaId=0802&sessionId=22977\nDetails: http
 s://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/28/the-apartment-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7562198;-122.419185
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35067999/1b61c3e0-bcd1-4c16-98d7-ed042477d069.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261029T100747Z
LOCATION:Alamo Drafthouse Cinema\, 2550 Mission St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 
 94110
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/28/the-apartment-tickets
END:VEVENT
